From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] lxc: bind the host GNSS socket directory into the container

A vendor GNSS HAL (android/gnss-hal) reads NMEA from
/run/waydroid-gnss/nmea.sock on the host, which bcm4776-gnssd serves
with group gps (1021). Bind the directory to /dev/waydroid-gnss when it
exists. The session config is rewritten on every session start, so this
needs no "waydroid upgrade".
---
--- a/tools/helpers/lxc.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/lxc.py
@@ -209,6 +209,13 @@
     if not make_entry(session["waydroid_data"], "data", options="rbind 0 0"):
         raise OSError("Failed to bind userdata")
 
+    # Host GNSS: a vendor GNSS HAL reads NMEA from a socket in this
+    # directory (group gps, so apps can't). Regenerated per session, so it
+    # follows the host service without a "waydroid upgrade".
+    gnss_dir = "/run/waydroid-gnss"
+    if os.path.isdir(gnss_dir):
+        make_entry(gnss_dir, "dev/waydroid-gnss", options="bind,create=dir,optional 0 0")
+
     lxc_path = tools.config.defaults["lxc"] + "/waydroid"
     config_nodes_tmp_path = args.work + "/config_session"
     with open(config_nodes_tmp_path, "w") as f:
